# Generated benchmark output (regenerate with scripts in benchmarks/)
# Result JSONs are intentionally tracked: the most recent run is committed
# back to the repo by .github/workflows/benchmark.yml so performance is
# permanent, auditable, and visible in the README — not stuck in
# 90-day-expiring CI artifacts.  Visualisations (PNG) stay generated.
results/latest/
benchmarks/*.png

# Empirical comparison harness output (benchmarks/empirical_benchmark.py): an
# on-demand, user-reproducible CI artifact (uploaded, not committed) — keep it
# out of the repo so it stays lean. Regenerate with
# `python -m benchmarks.empirical_benchmark --readme-subset`.
benchmarks/empirical_benchmark_results.json
benchmarks/empirical_benchmark_report.md
benchmarks/EMPIRICAL_BENCHMARK_REPORT.md

# Generated report files (CI artifacts)
live-data-report.json
bandit-report.json
safety-report.json
pip-audit-report.json
semgrep-report.json

